CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* alias template CTAD: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
g++ 13 (-fsanitize=address,undefined) accepts this program and it fails only
its WRONG assertion; clang++ 18 lacks alias-template CTAD (added in 19).
Fixed: "found no match for symbol 'Q'"; class template argument
deduction now handles an alias template whose defining-type-id is a
simple-template-id (deduce_alias_template_arguments).
